@startuml Concurrent Allocation Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"

actor "User A\n(Client)" as UserA #AliceBlue
actor "User B\n(Client)" as UserB #AliceBlue
participant "API Gateway /\nSearch Service" as API #LightGreen
database "Database\n(Lottery DB)" as DB #Lavender
participant "Redis\n(Distributed Lock)" as Redis #Pink


UserA -> API: 1. Search pattern: 1****5
UserB -> API: 2. Search pattern: 1****5

group Concurrency Control (User A)
    API -> Redis: 3. Acquire lock (pattern: 1****5)
    Redis --> API: 4. Lock acquired (TTL)

    API -> DB: 5. Query available tickets (using index)
    activate DB
    DB -> DB: 6. Find matching tickets (not allocated)
    DB --> API: 7. Return candidate ticket IDs
    deactivate DB

    API -> DB: 8. Reserve ticket (atomic update: set allocated = true)
    activate DB
    DB --> API: 9. Success (ticket ID)
    deactivate DB

    API -> Redis: 10. Release lock
    Redis --> API: 11. Lock released
end

API --> UserA: 12. Return ticket to User A

note over API, UserB
  สำหรับ User B: Acquire Lock ต่อเนื่อง
  -> ข้ามสลากของ A -> จัดสรรสลากใบถัดไป
end note

API --> UserB: 13. Return next available ticket to User B

@enduml
